<<
/Title (A recursive verifier calls itself for the next valid attempt. It has O\(a\) time and O\(a\) call-stack space for a attempts; loops use O\(1\) auxiliary space. Recursion adds stack overhead and is unnecessary for a small bounded retry process.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 597 0 R
>>
endobj
631 0 obj
<<
/Title (Strings are immutable, so upper\(\) returns a new string and leaves the original unchanged. For a 9-character registration, s[-4:] returns the final four digits and s[4:-4] returns one series letter. For a 10-character registration, the same slices return four digits and two series letters.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 600 0 R
>>
endobj
